# ButtonsCLI shell integration for zsh: OSC 133 marks (A prompt start,
# C command start, D;<exit code> finished). ButtonsCLI sets ZDOTDIR to a
# folder whose startup files load yours first; this file then adds the
# hooks and points ZDOTDIR back at your folder.
# To use it over SSH or in a shell ButtonsCLI did not start, source it from
# ~/.zshrc (the guard keeps it from loading twice).
if [[ -n "$BUTTONSCLI_SHELL_INTEGRATION" ]]; then
    # Started by ButtonsCLI: load your .zshrc from your own folder first.
    unset BUTTONSCLI_SHELL_INTEGRATION
    __bcli_home="${BUTTONSCLI_USER_ZDOTDIR:-$HOME}"
    unset BUTTONSCLI_USER_ZDOTDIR
    ZDOTDIR="$__bcli_home"
    [[ -r "$__bcli_home/.zshrc" ]] && . "$__bcli_home/.zshrc"
    # Later startup files (.zlogin) and child shells use your own folder.
    if [[ "$__bcli_home" == "$HOME" ]]; then
        unset ZDOTDIR
    else
        ZDOTDIR="$__bcli_home"
    fi
    unset __bcli_home
fi
if [[ -z "$__bcli_loaded" && -o interactive ]]; then
    __bcli_loaded=1
    __bcli_ran=
    __bcli_precmd() {
        local code=$?
        if [[ -n "$__bcli_ran" ]]; then
            printf '\033]133;D;%s\007' "$code"
        fi
        __bcli_ran=
        printf '\033]133;A\007'
        return $code
    }
    __bcli_preexec() {
        __bcli_ran=1
        printf '\033]133;C\007'
    }
    precmd_functions=(__bcli_precmd $precmd_functions)
    preexec_functions+=(__bcli_preexec)
fi
